+# CSE-CIC-IDS2018 Network Security AI integration
+
+## Existing contracts and implementation
+
+This adds opt-in, local inference under `security_ai/network/v4`, alongside the existing
+CICIDS2017 XGBoost classifier. It reuses `FeatureSchema`, `FeatureSet`, checked source
+provenance, the `SecurityAI` wrapper, model registry, `SecurityAIPrediction`, `AISignal`,
+and `Evidence`. The existing CICIDS2017 extractor and preprocessing remain unchanged;
+their smaller feature contract cannot consume these 40 flow features.
+
+The adapter contains no tool registry, executor, policy engine, approval manager, LLM,
+or incident mutation capability. Existing `SecurityAIInvestigator` can run its registered
+wrapper; failures remain typed/failed investigation steps, never benign predictions.
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    Flow[Precomputed CIC-IDS2018 Top40 flow] --> Extract[Top40FeatureExtractor + checked provenance]
+    Extract --> Adapter[NetworkSecurityAIAdapter / registered SecurityAI]
+    Adapter --> Quality[detection_quality: LightGBM V4-B2]
+    Adapter --> Edge[edge: DNN FP32]
+    Quality --> Prediction[Normalized prediction]
+    Edge --> Prediction
+    Prediction --> Signal[AISignal: model-derived context]
+    Prediction --> Receipt[Evidence: receipt of model run, attack unconfirmed]
+    Receipt --> Assessor[ThreatAssessor: hypotheses + advisory assessment]
+    Assessor --> Investigation[Further read-only investigation]
+    Investigation --> Policy[Existing Policy Engine]
+    Policy --> Approval[Existing human approval for WRITE]
+    Approval --> Execution[Existing governed execution]
+```
+
+A receipt is source-confirmed evidence **that inference occurred**, not source-confirmed
+evidence that the predicted attack occurred. It explicitly carries `model_derived=true`,
+`attack_confirmed=false`, and `confidence_calibrated=false`; reliability remains unknown.
+The assessment validator rejects observations referencing these receipts. Hypotheses and
+advisory summaries may reference them. No `IncidentState` severity/confidence is changed
+by inference. The existing 4096-character per-evidence and 64000-character total assessment
+budgets remain enforced. Metadata is allowlisted; the raw Top40 vector is not copied.
+
+Existing fusion support still accepts `AISignal` via its normal trusted composition; this
+change does not automatically ensemble two backends or reinterpret their confidence.
+
+## Profiles and configuration
+
+| Profile | Backend | Full Validation Macro F1 | Purpose |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| `detection_quality` | LightGBM V4-B2 | 0.808655 | SOC/server detection quality |
+| `edge` | DNN FP32, checkpoint epoch 13 | 0.698647 | Small model / low-latency CPU candidate |
+
+These are CSE-CIC-IDS2018 **development Validation** results, not production/drone
+performance. The higher DNN Accuracy does not imply better minority detection. Test V2
+was consumed at V3; integration does not access Test, train, tune or modify models.
+TorchAO INT8 remains experimental and is not supported as a production profile or a
+mandatory dependency. Its existing artifacts are not changed.
+
+`NetworkSecurityAIConfig` is a frozen Pydantic configuration model, supplied explicitly
+by trusted application setup; this repository has no global application CLI/settings router
+to extend. Defaults are disabled and `detection_quality`; no confidence threshold is added.
+There is no silent fallback to another model or to a benign prediction.
+
+```python
+from pathlib import Path
+from soc_agent.security_ai import SecurityAIRegistry, create_ai_signal
+from soc_agent.security_ai.network.v4 import (
+    NetworkSecurityAIConfig,
+    Top40FeatureExtractor,
+    create_network_security_ai,
+    prediction_to_evidence,
+)
+
+config = NetworkSecurityAIConfig(
+    enabled=True,
+    profile="detection_quality",  # or "edge"
+    artifact_root=Path("../ML"),  # supplied by application setup, relative to working directory
+)
+adapter = create_network_security_ai(config)
+registry = SecurityAIRegistry()
+if adapter is not None:
+    registry.register(adapter.as_security_ai())
+```
+
+Only the selected backend loads, at first inference, with a per-predictor cache and lock
+for concurrent first use. Importing this module loads neither torch nor lightgbm nor model
+weights. A predictor lifetime belongs to the application, not to each request. CPU inference
+runs through `asyncio.to_thread` to avoid blocking the investigation event loop. Cancelling
+an await does not interrupt an already-running native CPU call; it does not initiate response.
+
+## Artifact contract
+
+All paths below are configurable, project-relative and contained under `artifact_root`.
+Absolute artifact subpaths, parent traversal and escaping symlinks are rejected.
+
+| Artifact | Default relative path |
+|---|---|
+| Ordered features | `results/feature_selection/top40_features.csv` |
+| Original class-to-ID mapping | `data/processed/network_ml/label_mapping.json` |
+| LightGBM | `models/network/lightgbm_top40_v4b2.txt` |
+| DNN checkpoint | `models/network/dnn_top40_v4_best.pt` |
+| Trained scaler | `models/network/dnn_top40_v4_scaler.joblib` |
+
+The ordered Top40 CSV and label mapping load once when the enabled adapter is created.
+Mapping is read from the original artifact; no attack labels/IDs are redefined in code.
+The bundled `artifact_manifest.json` pins SHA256 of the actual reviewed model, scaler,
+feature and mapping files. Model/scaler checks happen once at lazy load, before deserialization;
+metadata checks happen once at enabled adapter creation. A changed V4-A model cannot be
+silently relabeled V4-B2. Trusted administrators can configure `bundle_manifest_path`
+relative to `artifact_root` to provision an explicitly reviewed replacement/test bundle.
+Contract digests cover ordered feature names and mapping bytes. A digest records identity;
+it is not a signature or authentication of a model package. Admins must provision compatible
+model/scaler/mapping files as a trusted bundle. Pickled scalers can execute code: never load
+untrusted/uploaded artifacts. `torch.load(weights_only=True, map_location="cpu")` is used
+for this checkpoint; model state is loaded strictly and its Top40 order/epoch are checked.
+LightGBM's serialized feature names replace spaces with underscores; this is explicitly
+validated. Scaler count, means, scales and named feature order (when present) are checked.
+
+Large models/datasets are not copied into this repository or committed. Store provisioned
+bundles under the existing ignored `/artifacts/` path, preserving/configuring their layout,
+or reference the separately managed ML project root. Small tests include exact copied
+feature/mapping metadata, fake model/scaler loaders, and no operational traffic.
+
+## Input and preprocessing
+
+Input must contain exactly Top40 keys. Ordering is the adapter's responsibility. Numeric
+scalars and numeric strings are converted to float32; booleans, nonnumeric input, missing/
+extra keys and finite float32 overflow fail explicitly. NaN/±Inf/None normalize to missing.
+For JSON/provenance use `null` or numeric strings `"NaN"`/`"Infinity"`, not nonstandard JSON
+NaN tokens. `Top40FeatureExtractor` normalizes missing to JSON `null`, matching the existing
+strict finite-or-null `FeatureSet` contract. It requires a versioned
+`cse_cic_ids2018_flow` source containing **precomputed** Top40 flow features and validates
+source incident/evidence binding. It does not derive CIC flow features from packets.
+
+LightGBM receives canonical float32 and missing NaN, without a scaler. Its V4 training
+notebook uses raw Top40 float32. DNN uses NaN → trained `scaler.mean_` → `scaler.transform`
+→ float32 → CPU eval/inference mode → softmax. Production torch thread settings remain owned by the
+application; the adapter does not mutate process-global torch thread counts. Never call fit/fit_transform in production.
+This reproduces `scripts/benchmark_model_memory.py` preprocessing and the checkpoint
+architecture. The DNN training notebook is empty in the current ML checkout, so training
+provenance cannot be fully audited; the existing trained scaler/checkpoint are reused.
+
+## Probability, failure and telemetry semantics
+
+Confidence is raw argmax class probability; `threat_score = 1 - P(Benign)`. LightGBM
+multiclass probabilities and DNN softmax are validated as finite `(1,15)` values in `[0,1]`
+with sum≈1. They are not calibrated probabilities of a real attack. No score is converted
+to incident severity, approval, WRITE permission or a response action.
+
+`inference_latency_ms` is actual per-call elapsed time around backend loading/preprocessing/
+forward (cold loading on first use), excluding feature validation/extraction. It is not the
+pure-forward benchmark number; no benchmark is hardcoded into runtime. Structured logging
+uses backend/version/success/latency and success class/confidence, without input features,
+flow payload, IP identifiers, exception messages or stack contents. Integrators configure
+the standard logging handlers as elsewhere in the application.
+
+Missing/corrupt/incompatible artifacts, invalid input, invalid probabilities and runtime
+failure raise existing `SecurityAIError` subclasses or `NetworkArtifactError`. The existing
+wrapper/investigator records failure; callers must not substitute a benign result. Failed
+inference creates no success receipt. Raw exceptions are retained as Python causes for
+trusted debugging, not included in public receipts/log messages.
+
+## Demo and assessment integration
+
+Install only the selected optional dependency profile:
+
+```bash
+uv sync --extra network-quality
+PYTHONPATH=src uv run --extra network-quality python examples/network_v4/predict.py \
+  --input examples/network_v4/synthetic_flow.json \
+  --artifact-root ../ML --profile detection_quality
+
+uv sync --extra network-edge
+PYTHONPATH=src uv run --extra network-edge python examples/network_v4/predict.py \
+  --input examples/network_v4/synthetic_flow.json \
+  --artifact-root ../ML --profile edge
+```
+
+The fixture is an artificial ramp of feature values and has no ground-truth attack label.
+Its output demonstrates the schema/pipeline, not model accuracy or realistic traffic.
+The demo prints prediction and its inference receipt; it does not call an LLM or tools.
+For application integration:
+
+```python
+feature_set = Top40FeatureExtractor(adapter.predictor.contract).extract(record, state=state)
+result = await registry.get(adapter.predictor.model_name).predict(
+    {"incident_id": state.incident_id, "input": feature_set}
+)
+signal = create_ai_signal(
+    result, state=state, source_evidence_ids=feature_set.provenance.source_evidence_ids
+)
+receipt = prediction_to_evidence(result)
+state = state.add_evidence(receipt)  # explicit application ingestion, not adapter mutation
+analysis = await assessor.assess(state)  # injected existing ThreatAssessor/LLM
+# Further investigation/response planning use their existing coordinators.
+# Any proposed WRITE still passes PolicyEngine and exact human approval + GovernedExecutor.
+```
+
+Use only one profile per deployment. An externally ingested feature record must carry
+honest provenance; neither a model digest nor prediction establishes evidence authenticity.
+
+## Tests and limitations
+
+Run `uv run pytest`, `uv run ruff check .`, and `uv run ruff format --check .`.
+New unit/integration tests use fake local loaders/weights, verify canonical features,
+missing/invalid/nonfinite input, model/schema mismatch, caching, profile routing, bounded
+receipts, no observation promotion, and existing WRITE approval/destructive denial behavior.
+Optional real-artifact demo runs are separate from pytest and do not access Test V2.
+
+Remaining: actual production traffic validation, DNN minority-class weakness, SlowHTTP/FTP
+structural ambiguity, confidence calibration not completed, target embedded/ARM/NPU
+latency/RAM/power validation, and CIC-IDS2018→drone traffic generalization unverified.
+LightGBM has the higher Macro F1; FP32 is only the low-cost inference candidate. Serialized
+weight size is not process runtime RSS or a full deployment dependency footprint.
